# Checks are intentionally broad; targeted exclusions below are style choices, not suppressed bugs:
#  - modernize-use-trailing-return-type: the codebase uses leading return types.
#  - readability-identifier-length: short loop/lambda names (i, j, c) are idiomatic here.
#  - *-magic-numbers: card games are full of inherent constants (13 ranks, 4 suits, position math).
#  - readability-convert-member-functions-to-static / misc-use-internal-linkage: public API surface
#    is kept as member functions for the documented class interfaces.
#  - misc/cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes: Player deliberately shares
#    state with subclasses via protected members.
#  - cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access: every operator[] call is
#    bounds-checked by the surrounding logic, and the ASan/UBSan CI job verifies it at runtime;
#    the project does not depend on the GSL, so gsl::at is unavailable.
#  - altera-*, fuchsia-*, llvmlibc-*, etc. are not enabled (domain-specific profiles).
---
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -readability-convert-member-functions-to-static,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(include|tests)/.*'
FormatStyle: file
